in years to come when you're avoiding inpatient treatment and all the kind of crises that go with a young person with BPD. Does that same approach work with an adult who has BPD? I mean, let's say you're in a relationship with somebody who has a lot of these characteristics. characteristics, do you have to behave in that way in order to accommodate the way that they react? Absolutely, absolutely. So in the therapy approach that I use most often is called mentalization-based therapy. And this slowing down is really what we call the mentalizing stance. And the mentalizing stance is the stance that we take in order to help another person feel understood or
我们对BPD和BPD患者有太多错误的观念，要理解我们所有人都有自我和人际关系糟糕的日子。没有人能总是完美地管理他们的人际关系。这是我们每天面临的最大挑战。是的，患有BPD或人格障碍的人会有更多与人发生冲突的时刻，但我们所有人都能感同身受，将这一点放在同一个维度上，并承认典型和非典型人格功能之间的连续性，这就是我们需要前进的方向。

