00:29:28.000 --> 00:30:26.000
validated. If you use DBT language, you would say you make another person feel validated. In MBT language, mentalization-based therapy language, we say we make a person feel understood. People with BPD have almost an existential feeling of being misunderstood. They feel very alienated, not only from society, from their family members, but also from themselves. They don't feel homie in their own bodies. They don't feel comfortable in their own bodies and it's a very, very lonely existence. And so what family members can do and therapists for people with BPD is to help them feel understood. And we only help people feel understood when we slow down. And when we put our mind on the table and say, you know, this is a dilemma for me. On the one hand, I feel I want to help you with this.
得到验证。如果你使用DBT（辩证行为疗法）的术语，你会说你让另一个人感到被验证。在MBT（心智化临床治疗）的术语中，我们说我们让一个人感到被理解。边缘型人格障碍（BPD）患者几乎有一种存在主义式的被误解感。他们感到非常疏离，不仅是与社会、与家人疏离，甚至与他们自己也感到疏离。他们在自己的身体里感到不自在。他们在自己的身体里感到不舒服，这是一种非常、非常孤独的存在状态。因此，家人和治疗师能为BPD患者所做的，就是帮助他们感到被理解。而我们只有在放慢节奏时，才能帮助人们感到被理解。当我们把自己的想法摆在桌面上，说：你知道，这对我来说是一个两难的境地。一方面，我觉得我想在这件事上帮助你。

43
00:30:26.000 --> 00:30:59.000
on the other hand, I feel I don't want to interfere with what you're busy with. Where does that leave us? In putting your mind on the table like that, in explaining rather than jumping to conclusions or taking shortcuts, you instill in the recipient of your communication a feeling of being understood. So absolutely, you're absolutely right, Kim, for both for children, but also for adults in our lives, but also therapists. We slow down. it's the only way to go with people with with BPD.
另一方面，我觉得我不想干涉你正在忙的事情。这让我们处于什么境地？通过这样把你的想法摆在桌面上，通过解释而不是妄下结论或走捷径，你会在沟通的接收者心中灌输一种被理解的感觉。所以绝对没错，金，无论是对孩子，还是对我们生活中的成年人，甚至是治疗师，都是如此。我们放慢节奏，这是与BPD患者相处的唯一途径。

